    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d843">

                <pb facs="d842-4" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d842-4"/>

                <head>843. Telegram 182 to Prague<anchor n="1" xml:id="d843-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1957-11-21">November 21,
                        1957</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d843-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d843-1"/>
                <p>182. For Ambassador Only. Your tel 297.</p>
                <p>We agree you should go ahead with December 12 meeting.</p>
                <p>Would like your comment on following alternative methods continuing talks under
                    consideration here: 1) Beam meet with Wang in Warsaw, 2) Rankin commute Geneva from Belgrade following
                    assignment there, 3) talks be continued at lower level and conducted by
                        Martin commuting to Geneva.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d843-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d843-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/11–2157. Confidential;
                    Priority; Limit Distribution. Drafted by Clough; cleared by Howe (S/S), Henderson (O), and Elbrick (EUR).
                    The time of transmission is illegible.</p>
            </note>
